<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F0070979>.
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Stochastical analysis of laser tracker data - shown for the Leica AT960-LR".
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "To analyse the stochastic properties of the laser tracker Leica AT960-LR, five fix points spatially distributed were continuously observed from three different positions in the 3D laboratory of the Geodetic Institute Hanover, Leibniz University Hanover. Each of the five fix points was measured at each position with the measuring rates 1 Hz, 10 Hz, 20 Hz, 100 Hz and 1000 Hz for ten minutes each. For detailed information on the data sets and data acquisition please read the document  __“Data_Description.pdf”__.   This data set and its analyses are part the project \\'Bayesian adaptive robust adjustment of multivariate geodetic measurement processes with data gaps and nonstationary colored noise\\' (project number 386369985) funded by the German Research Foundation (DFG).".
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010".
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:22:01.601640"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:22:01.601648"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/geodaetisches-institut-hannover>.
<http://localhost:5002/5feb8f99-2824-4b4a-9a97-403c28655010> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double>.
