<http://localhost:5002/b679d6a2-fe5e-42ce-962a-89aa39260496> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:b679d6a2-fe5e-42ce-962a-89aa39260496.
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F0084372>.
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Surface roughness of real operationally used compressor blade and blisk".
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The data set contains three dimensional measured surfaces of real worn  compressor blades from real mid-sized air craft engine high pressure coompressors. Three stages of the compressor are measured. The first stage, the centre stage and the last stage.  Also surface data of a real worn Blisk from a small aircraft engine will be published. We are currently preparing the data.  Further information of the data are given in: Gilge, P.; Kellersmann, A.; Friedrichs, J.; Seume J.R. (2019): Surface roughness of real operationally used compressor blade and blisk. Proceedings of the Institution of Mechanical Engineers, Part G: Journal of Aerospace Engineering, https://doi.org/10.1177/0954410019843438".
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620".
<http://localhost:5002/d0b83f6d-dd19-4629-98b9-99d17aeee620> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:23:29.283855"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
