<http://localhost:5002/95c378f5-3673-4652-a67f-6dd2086da48e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/95c378f5-3673-4652-a67f-6dd2086da48e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F7p6wv6cg>.
<http://localhost:5002/95c378f5-3673-4652-a67f-6dd2086da48e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Additive manufacturing data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens".
<http://localhost:5002/95c378f5-3673-4652-a67f-6dd2086da48e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset was generated in the context of a parameter study in the paper: _Supplementary data of “Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Influence of process parameters on interface formation in in-plane 316L/CuCrZr laser powder bed fusion\\'_   It includes: 1. Design data, 2. Preparation data, 3. In-situ camera snapshots, 4. Physical photos after manufacturing  * __Materials:__ 316L (Carpenter Additive) and CuCrZr (Eckart TLS GmbH) * __Design:__ Autodesk Inventor Professional 2022 * __Data preparation:__ Autodesk Netfabb Ultimate 2021 * __PBF-LB Machine:__ Aconity MIDI+ equipped with an integrated Aerosint SPD Recoater V1.0 * __Software:__ AconitySTUDIO * __Process monitoring:__ High-speed CMOS camera  ![ Arrangement of the 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens on the build platform for the parameter study]( https://data.uni-hannover.de/de/dataset/8062e5f1-c882-477d-8f4a-43fbdd8b3490/resource/5ac01325-a503-44b4-bd9c-b049735158b2/download/arrangement_specimens_build-platform.png) Arrangement of the 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens on the build platform for the parameter study  ### References  Meyer, I., Oel, M., Ehlers, T., & Lachmayer, R. (2023). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Design guidelines for manufacturing of 316L/CuCrZr in laser powder bed fusion*. Heliyon, 9(8), e18301. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e18301  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *µCT data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/bi1jbiq9  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *Light microscopy data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/rsjz3w2k  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *SEM data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/wan2sabi  ### Acknowledgments  The project ”*Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung*” was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7-87011865.  The project ”*Major Research Instrumentation for integration of efficient effects in multi-material structural components*” was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG - German Research Foundation) - Project number 445707542.".
