<http://localhost:5002/ca4b6ad9-5cd3-45b5-85a3-3f2f5b69c97f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/ca4b6ad9-5cd3-45b5-85a3-3f2f5b69c97f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fv3s7egah>.
<http://localhost:5002/ca4b6ad9-5cd3-45b5-85a3-3f2f5b69c97f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "INSAR_stochastic".
<http://localhost:5002/ca4b6ad9-5cd3-45b5-85a3-3f2f5b69c97f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Reference implementation of the three-component spectral stochastic model for the InSAR differential phase (Kermarrec, submitted to IEEE TGRS). The model decomposes the radial 2D periodogram into a two-regime Von Karman atmospheric spectrum, a k^-3 orbital/ionospheric residual, and a thermal noise plateau, fitted per pair and inverted frequency-by-frequency in the BLUE. The package contains the full spectral SBAS pipeline, the standalone BLUE solver, the reference baseline methods (Cao 2018, Duan-tau, STOMAC), and a self-contained synthetic demo that verifies the calibration properties (sigma_apo^2 = 1, rate-domain Cal = 1) without any input data. Provided for peer review. Files to generate the figures are provided".
