<http://localhost:5002/9f6e8bae-bf47-4abf-867b-4ed5d859d9ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:9f6e8bae-bf47-4abf-867b-4ed5d859d9ad.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F0027803>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "LUMO - Leibniz University Test Structure for Monitoring".
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The published dataset comprises long-term structural measurements of a lattice tower to support and facilitate the research in the field of Structural Health Monitoring (SHM). The structure is located near Hanover in Northern Germany and is equipped with reversible damage mechanisms on multiple positions, which have been repeatedly activated and reactivated during the measurement period from August, 2020 to Juli, 2021.   Meteorological measurements have been conducted in parallel by the Institute of Meteorology and Climatology (IMUK) of Leibniz University Hannover and are provided in the same file format as the structural data.  For unlocking the meteorological data, please send an informal request to *public.data(at)isd.uni-hannover.de*.".
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9".
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:08:03.583755"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:08:03.583760"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fur-statik-und-dynamik>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/lumo>.
<http://localhost:5002/037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:037fd03c-299d-47b4-a9ac-9a1cd325d2c9.
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Faq5cdmx7>.
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Spectral BRDF measurements and fitted reflection model parameters of ten urban materials".
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset provides laboratory BRDF measurements of ten materials representing common surface types in a Central European urban environment: flat roofing tiles, roofing felt, asphalt, four types of clinker brick slips, and three types of render. Measurements were performed with a gonioreflectometer at the Institute for Solar Energy Research Hamelin (ISFH), sampling each material at 1264 angular configurations over the wavelength range 400–1030 nm. The samples are treated as isotropic, which motivates an asymmetric sampling scheme with a small set of incident directions, each combined with a large number of outgoing directions. The dataset comprises spectrally resolved and AM1.5G-weighted BRDF values, the numerically calculated surface albedo, and the fitted parameters of three energy-normalized analytical reflection models (Lambertian, Phong, and energy-preserving Oren-Nayar), which allow the measured reflectance to be used directly in ray-tracing simulations.  ### Related publication \\'Spectral BRDF measurements and reflectance modeling of urban materials: An open dataset\\', submitted to _Advances in Applied Energy_. For a detailed description of the measurement setup, data processing, model fitting, and findings, see the publication. Please cite this dataset when using the data, and the publication when referring to the methodology or reported findings.  ### Dataset structure The data are organized as four CSV files: the spectrally resolved BRDF, the AM1.5G-weighted BRDF, the fitted reflection model parameters, and a materials table listing the sample names, descriptions, and categories. All BRDF values are given in 1/sr, all reflection model parameters are dimensionless, and all angles are given in degrees. Photographs of the material samples are provided in the material_pictures folder.  ### Acknowledgements This work was financially supported by the German Federal Ministry of Economic Affairs and Energy (BMWE) under the grant number 03EE1187D (DIGI-PV).".
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719".
<http://localhost:5002/f852f438-1a12-4cc6-9411-b672480a5719> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:20:58.234500"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
