<http://localhost:5002/82b1c3c6-bf66-4469-92c1-5bb6a7635b67> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Flyav246d>.
<http://localhost:5002/82b1c3c6-bf66-4469-92c1-5bb6a7635b67> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "A benchmark structure for virtual sensing on tower structures".
<http://localhost:5002/82b1c3c6-bf66-4469-92c1-5bb6a7635b67> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset contains experimental measurement data of a 1.52 m vertical cantilever beam. The beam is equipped with DC-capable accelerations sensor and laser displacement sensors at three measuring points as well as electrical strain gauges at two measuring points.  The excitation is carried out by manually applying a displacement boundary condition to the top of the beam, consisting of three distinct parts: stepwise static displacements, a free decay, and a quasi-random excitation with high energy content in the quasi-static frequency range.".
