<http://localhost:5002/a25e679e-1395-4faf-b3dd-8f7b73d759ab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:a25e679e-1395-4faf-b3dd-8f7b73d759ab.
<http://localhost:5002/157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fvgrg4moe>.
<http://localhost:5002/157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "µCT data of an additively manufactured demonstrator with inner lattice channels for use in heat exchangers".
<http://localhost:5002/157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains micro-computed tomography images of an additively manufactured (powder bed fusion of metals using a laser beam, PBF-LB/M) demonstrator part intended for thermal applications. The part consists of branching internal fluid channels and has been generated via _Algorithms-Aided Design_ using the software _Grasshopper_.  * __Outer Dimensions:__ 30 x 29 x 56 mm³ * __Wall Thickness:__ 0.6 mm * __Channel Diameters:__ 	* 4 mm (Inner Channels) 	* 8 mm (Inlet + Outlet) * __Material:__ 1.2709 (MS1) * __PBF-LB Machine:__ EOS EOSINT M 280 * __µCT Scanner:__ Bruker SkyScan 1275  ![Volumetric Representation](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/360098ca-9e6f-47ef-8ca5-aec6acb8a278/resource/019ca72d-c462-4497-bd9b-1bc3ff388858/download/ct_50_um_rec0000_voi_a.png ) Volumetric representation of the obtained CT data  ### References:  This data was obtained in the context of the bachelor thesis:  * Messmann, C. O.: _Generation of Biomimetic Structures to Increase the Thermal Performance of Additively Manufactured Heat Exchangers_, 2022, Leibniz University Hannover  ### Acknowledgements:  * The project _“Computer tomograph for optomechatronic systems”_ was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) - Project number 432176896.".
<http://localhost:5002/157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "157efa97-bc92-4009-9c8a-d2d0cab4160a".
