<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F6c8ysz7v>.
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CAD data and simulation results for a study on thermal management in multi-material microreactors".
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "# Description This data set contains the CAD files of 12 different multi-material microchannel reactors for ammonia decomposition. The designs are intended for additive manufacturing on an Aconity MIDI+ equipped with an Aerosint Selective Powder Deposition Recoater V1.0 (or similar machines). The CAD data is available in manufacturer-neutral .step file format. CFD simulations were performed in Ansys Fluent using these designs. The raw data from these simulations are included in this data set in neutral .csv format.  #References The research data was used in the following publication: https://doi.org/10.1017/pds.2026.10559  # Acknowledgements This work is part of the project “Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung”, which was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7–87011865.".
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b".
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T09:50:29.429823"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T09:50:29.429838"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fur-produktentwicklung-und-geratebau>.
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/cad-data-and-simulation-results-for-a-study-on-thermal-management-in-multi-material-microreactors>.
<http://localhost:5002/2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:2d2dcd80-eeb0-4afc-be32-164e1a48752b.
<http://localhost:5002/fe530abf-16d1-42f5-bf86-dfa4d711062d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/fe530abf-16d1-42f5-bf86-dfa4d711062d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Feoiog0ot>.
<http://localhost:5002/fe530abf-16d1-42f5-bf86-dfa4d711062d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Nanosecond-Pulsed Laser Ablation as a Universal  Method for Oxide Removal and Surface Structuring of Aluminum and Copper for Advanced Manufacturing Applications".
<http://localhost:5002/fe530abf-16d1-42f5-bf86-dfa4d711062d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains all relevant files for the publication: \\'Nanosecond-Pulsed Laser Ablation as a Universal  Method for Oxide Removal and Surface Structuring of Aluminum and Copper for Advanced Manufacturing Applications\\'  # Dataset description The Data is available in the original processing formats.  ## CLSM - Roughness measurements - CLSM-Data of aluminum and copper samples in .vk6-Format   - Exported Pictures   - Excel-Files of exported roughness values (Sa, Sq, Sz, Sp, Sv, Sal, Sdq, Sdr, Std, Str, Spd, Spc) - Python-Scripts for Plotting  ## Nanoindentation - Excel-Files of Nanoindentation measurements - Python-Script for Plotting  ## XRD - Residual Stresses: Raw-Data from XRD-Measurements on aluminum and copper samples - Texture: Raw-Data from XRD-Measurements on aluminum and copper samples - Python-Script for Plotting  ## XPS - Raw-Data and Plots of XPS measurements of aluminum and copper samples  ## Data from the Section \\'Applications in Manufacturing\\' Data used to generate plots in the application-section of the paper with the following manufacturing processes:    * Adhesive bonding   - Cold roll bonding   - Compound casting   - Laser beam brazing     # Citation Janthur, Finn-Lennard and Seffer, Sarah and Hermsdorf, Jörg and Barienti, Khemais and Heimers, Henri and Steinhoff, Timon and Nürnberger, Florian and Klose, Christian and Herbst, Sebastian and Maier, Hans Jürgen and Kuhr, Lara and Raumel, Selina and Wurz, Marc and Gerland, Sandra and Raatz, Annika and Zimmermann, Sascha and Bürger, Friedrich and Gustus, René and Maus-Friedrichs, Wolfgang and Overmeyer, Ludger, \\'Nanosecond-Pulsed Laser Ablation as a Universal Method for Oxide Removal and Surface Structuring of Aluminum and Copper for Advanced Manufacturing Applications\\', vol. 34, pp. 101018, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsadv.2026.101018   # Funding Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) – Project-ID 394563137 – SFB 1368.   Open access funding enabled and organized by Projekt DEAL.".
