<http://localhost:5002/c7c0e643-f1a8-4ce2-ba2f-543e1deab695> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "How to Build an Optical Filter with an Atomic Vapor Cell".
<http://localhost:5002/c7c0e643-f1a8-4ce2-ba2f-543e1deab695> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The manuscript \\'How to Build an Optical Filter with an Atomic Vapor Cell\\' introduces two filter types - the Doppler and the Faraday filter. The Doppler filter acts barely on the absorption of resonant light. In the Faraday case, linear polarized light undergoes a magnetically induced rotation close to interatomic transition. The uploaded files contain two complete sets of data - one for the Doppler and one for the Faraday filter.".
<http://localhost:5002/c7c0e643-f1a8-4ce2-ba2f-543e1deab695> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "c7c0e643-f1a8-4ce2-ba2f-543e1deab695".
