<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fnz9zlhkh>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Callinstrasse Campus 3DGS Datensatz".
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Dieser Datensatz umfasst einen 3D-Gaussian-Splatting-Datensatz, ein zugehöriges Bildset sowie eine COLMAP-Datenbank mit den Ground-Truth-Posen der aufgenommenen Bilder. Die Aufnahmen zeigen den Parkplatzbereich zwischen dem Hochhaus und der Callinstraße rund um den Einsteinelevator. Die Bilder wurden mit zwei unterschiedlichen Kamerasystemen erfasst; zusätzlich enthält der Datensatz ein kleines Teilset mit schneebedeckter Szene. Der Datensatz eignet sich für die Evaluierung und Entwicklung von Verfahren zur Lokalisierung.".
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5".
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T09:50:51.137797"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T09:50:51.137804"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fur-kartographie-und-geoinformatik>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/callinstrasse-campus-3dgs-datensatz>.
<http://localhost:5002/afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:afa04d64-b847-4e86-b60d-7676644da6d5.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fl047b9xo>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Comparative data of ImageJ and MultiPoroX".
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset was generated in the context of a comparative analysis of the performance of defect analysis methods in the paper: _Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – A tool for automated defect analysis_.   __Used software:__ MATLAB® R2024b, ImageJ (Version 1.54p 17 February 2025)  For both analyses the same images and parameters were used.  __Used parameters:__  * __Resizing:__ None * __Scaling factor (Pixels per Milimeter):__ 840 * __Preprocessing:__ Histogram Equalization (1%) * __Segmentation Threshold:__ 65  __The analysis compared the results related to:__  * Calculated Porosity * Detected Defects * Unassigned Material Area * Unassigned Defect Area * Number of Unassigned Defects  ![Comparison of the reference analysis using ImageJ (IMJ) and MultiPoroX (MPX)](https://data.uni-hannover.de/de/dataset/f8ae6c67-36bc-4e6d-9da4-dce850f0104f/resource/75accf70-7bb0-4732-a4aa-bcac307cde18/download/comparison_of_the_reference_analysis_using_imagej_and_multiporox.svg)  Comparison of the reference analysis using ImageJ (IMJ) and MultiPoroX (MPX)   ### References Meyer, I., Glitt, L., Lachmayer, R. (2025). *MultiPoroX*: Automated multi-material porosity analysis tool [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/27xsmm9e  Meyer, I., Oel, M., Ehlers, T., & Lachmayer, R. (2023). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Design guidelines for manufacturing of 316L/CuCrZr in laser powder bed fusion*. Heliyon, 9(8), e18301. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e18301   ### Acknowledgments  The project ”*Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung*” was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7-87011865.  The project ”*Major Research Instrumentation for integration of efficient effects in multi-material structural components*” was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG - German Research Foundation) - Project number 445707542.".
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced".
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T09:53:07.388728"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T09:53:07.388736"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fur-produktentwicklung-und-geratebau>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/comparative-data-of-imagej-and-multiporox>.
<http://localhost:5002/53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:53a51bce-4596-439f-9721-88840b0bdced.
<http://localhost:5002/ced5695c-0a9c-4aa5-b912-fc21420321ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/ced5695c-0a9c-4aa5-b912-fc21420321ec> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fffwtmdgv>.
<http://localhost:5002/ced5695c-0a9c-4aa5-b912-fc21420321ec> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Dataset on wild flora diversity and associated agri-environmental information on organic legume fields in Tuscany (Italy)".
<http://localhost:5002/ced5695c-0a9c-4aa5-b912-fc21420321ec> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "__Study design__ This dataset contains sampling data from vegetation surveys conducted in 244 sample-plots within 32 lentil and chickpea fields across five organic farms situated in Tuscany, Italy. The sampling was conducted in summer 2022 and 2023. Wild flora was mapped in 1x2m sample-plots following drilled lines with a randomised sampling. Two strata (edge and centre) were sampled with four repetitions each. Furthermore, the dataset offers a detailed overview of the management practices implemented in each field, along with a description of site conditions including soil texture, organic matter content, local weather information during the legume growing period, and the diversity of the landscapes surrounding the fields.  __Dataset description__ The dataset is presented in a single workbook file comprising five sheets. Four of these sheets contain the essential dataset (general information, management details, environment, species list), while an extra sheet contains metadata providing descriptions of the variables. Each entry in the four core data tables corresponds to a sample-plot and is identified uniquely by an ID, which is a combination of two numbers. The whole number before the decimal point serves as the distinct field identifier, and the decimal number indicates the replicate number for the corresponding field. It\\'s worth noting that all sheets, excluding the metadata table, can be connected through the common ID field.  __Funding__ This study is funded by the Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF) (FKZ 01DH20007) under the PRIMA (Partnership for Research and Innovation in the Mediterranean Area) international funding initiative.  __Ethics Statement__ All farmers were informed about the purpose of this study and gave consent for participation and permission for visiting and surveying their fields. All collected data are anonymized.".
