<http://localhost:5002/6f3e7045-59db-4529-9019-3e6177cf82b7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:6f3e7045-59db-4529-9019-3e6177cf82b7.
<http://localhost:5002/d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F3h30e9di>.
<http://localhost:5002/d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "FuncCAD".
<http://localhost:5002/d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "FuncCAD is a dataset containing synthetically generated CAD-models. The geometry of the models have functional purpose. The CAD-models have been generated using Autodesk Inventor and their file format is IPT. Additionally all CAD-models are available in STEP-format. To add context information about the CAD-models, a JSON-file exists for each CAD-model. The JSON- and CAD-files have an identical name (aside from the file-ending). The JSON-files include information about design history and included features. Information about the features contains the feature-name, CAD-operations, which were used to create that feature, axis information if it is a rotationally symmetrical feature and shaft sections if it is a shaft.".
<http://localhost:5002/d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "d1521367-f71b-4794-aae5-f46c7a22693a".
