<http://localhost:5002/d21c0c06-60e6-4188-8286-a0e8d1f1dce8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fwan2sabi>.
<http://localhost:5002/d21c0c06-60e6-4188-8286-a0e8d1f1dce8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "SEM data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens".
<http://localhost:5002/d21c0c06-60e6-4188-8286-a0e8d1f1dce8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset was generated in the context of a parameter study in the paper: _Supplementary data of “Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Influence of process parameters on interface formation in in-plane 316L/CuCrZr laser powder bed fusion\\'_   It includes SEM data of seven specimens with the following sample numbers: 1, 8, 24, 25, 32, 33, 40.  * __Materials:__ 316L (Carpenter Additive) and CuCrZr (Eckart TLS GmbH) * __PBF-LB Machine:__ Aconity MIDI+ equipped with an integrated Aerosint SPD Recoater V1.0 * __Mounting material:__ AB-Zenopox * __Grinding machine:__ Struers Tegramin-30 * __SEM system:__ Zeiss SUPRA 55 VP  ![Exemplary scanning electron microscopy image of a 316L/CuCrZr multi-material sample (Sample 1)](https://data.uni-hannover.de/de/dataset/1d4cfae6-31a0-49f0-81d1-6d679e2fcd41/resource/2ae1bdea-56f4-40a9-a41f-9bd7102de35d/download/exemplary_sem_image_sample1.png) Exemplary scanning electron microscopy image of a 316L/CuCrZr multi-material sample (Sample 1)  ### References  Meyer, I., Oel, M., Ehlers, T., & Lachmayer, R. (2023). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Design guidelines for manufacturing of 316L/CuCrZr in laser powder bed fusion*. Heliyon, 9(8), e18301. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e18301  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *Additive manufacturing data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/7p6wv6cg  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *µCT data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/bi1jbiq9  Ina Meyer, Roland Lachmayer (2025). *Light microscopy data from a parameter study on 316L/CuCrZr multi-material specimens* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/rsjz3w2k  ### Acknowledgments  The project ”*Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung*” was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7-87011865.  The project ”*Major Research Instrumentation for integration of efficient effects in multi-material structural components*” was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG - German Research Foundation) - Project number 445707542.".
