<http://localhost:5002/91546c42-d71e-4bab-b3c6-0c96f88578e1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:91546c42-d71e-4bab-b3c6-0c96f88578e1.
<http://localhost:5002/53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F0089554>.
<http://localhost:5002/53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication Package: \\'How Does Usable Security (Not) End Up in Software Products? Results From a Qualitative Interview Study\\'".
<http://localhost:5002/53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Replication Package for the IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (Oakland \\'22) paper: \\'How Does Usable Security (Not) End Up in Software Products? Results From a Qualitative Interview Study\\'  To make our study reproducible and allow for easy access for meta-research, we publish a replication package containing the following documents:  (1) The pre-questionnaire for demographic and quantitative questions;  (2) The interview guide with the main questions and follow-up prompts for the semi-structured interviews;  (3) The materials we used to contact and recruit participants;  (4) The consent forms;  (5) A table of the software used in this study;  (6) The operationalized codebook with codes contributing to this paper.".
<http://localhost:5002/53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "53b84e37-c2d0-4588-bbd7-4c6f2fcc16ab".
