<http://localhost:5002/9efd1f00-c6d7-4e4f-b286-eb301527384f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/9efd1f00-c6d7-4e4f-b286-eb301527384f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fspxeaic7>.
<http://localhost:5002/9efd1f00-c6d7-4e4f-b286-eb301527384f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication Package: \\'If You Can’t Get Them to the Lab: Evaluating a Virtual Study Environment with Security Information Workers\\'".
<http://localhost:5002/9efd1f00-c6d7-4e4f-b286-eb301527384f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Replication Package for the Eighteenth Symposium on Usable Privacy and Security (SOUPS 2022) paper: “If You Can’t Get Them to the Lab: Evaluating a Virtual Study Environment with Security Information Workers”.  To make our study reproducible and allow for easy access for meta-research, we publish a replication package containing the following documents:  (1) study protocols for the cognitive walkthrough (2) the guided and the comparison study, including the study scenarios (3) the tasks descriptions (4) between-task surveys (5) end surveys".
