<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fin90p55t>.
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "GIS-based register of biogas plant sites in Lower Saxony, Germany".
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset contains a register of biogas plant sites in Lower Saxony with spatially-resolved and high up-to-date plant information. The register is intended to create a basis for identifying power-to-gas (P2G) potential for biogas plant sites. The dataset is being done within the context of the research project H2-FEE: Flexible energy carriers for the energy transition (running from July 2022 to presumably June 2025) funded by the Lower Saxony Investment and Development Bank (Investitions- und Förderbank Niedersachsen, NBank).".
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf".
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:01:37.184952"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:01:37.184958"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fur-umweltplanung>.
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/gis-based-register-of-biogas-plant-sites-in-lower-saxony-germany>.
<http://localhost:5002/4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:4d01d815-ef28-4d0a-9d68-d1bedff150cf.
<http://localhost:5002/09e95bfc-e25a-4973-baea-649de99153f4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/09e95bfc-e25a-4973-baea-649de99153f4> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fgo114ml5>.
<http://localhost:5002/09e95bfc-e25a-4973-baea-649de99153f4> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Water Sustainability Index Lower Saxony".
<http://localhost:5002/09e95bfc-e25a-4973-baea-649de99153f4> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset contains information on the Water Sustainability Index (WSI) of the groundwater sub-bodies in Lower Saxony for the periods 1991 - 2020 and 2021 - 2050. The WSI is based on the approach of Schlattmann et al. (2022) and is determined using the formula:  	WSI=  (Wirr+Wliv+Wind+Woth)/(WAt-(DWD+Wecos))  WSI = Water Sustainability Index; Wliv = Wasserbedarf Tierhaltende Betriebe (livestock production); Wirr = Wasserbedarf für Feldberegnung (irrigation); Wind = Industrieller Wasserbedarf (industrial); DWD = Öffentliche Wasserversorgung (domestic water demand); Woth = other water users; Wecos = Wasserbedarf für Biodiversität und Ökosysteme (ecosystem functioning); WAt = Grundwasserdargebot basierend auf mittlerer Grundwasserneubildung (total available water).  Our calculations of water demand for industry, agriculture, public water supply and others are based on authorized groundwater withdrawals for the period 2021–2027 from individual groundwater bodies (MU 2021). Additionally, we use projected abstraction volumes for the year 2050, derived from these baseline data (MU 2022). The data are available in cubic meters per year (m³/year).  The attribute table contains: - Mean groundwater recharge rate [m³/year] for the period 1991 – 2020 per sub-groundwater body  - Mean groundwater recharge rate [m³/year] for the period 2021 - 2050 per sub-groundwater body  - 15th percentile of the mean groundwater recharge rate [m³/year] for the period 2021 - 2050 per sub-groundwater body  - Annual withdrawals (m³/year) for the 2021 - 2027 and 2050 management period by user group (public water supply, field irrigation, livestock farms, industry, other)  German - Mittlere Grundwassserneubildungsrate [m³/Jahr] für den Betrachtungszeitraum 1991 - 2020 pro Teilgrundwasserkörper im Landkreis  - Mittlere Grundwassserneubildungsrate [m³/Jahr] für den Betrachtungszeitraum 2021 - 2050 pro Teilgrundwasserkörper im Landkreis  - 15er Perzentil der mittleren Grundwassserneubildungsrate [m³/Jahr] für den Betrachtungszeitraum 2021 - 2050 pro Teilgrundwasserkörper im Landkreis  - Jährliche Entnahmemenge (m³/Jahr) für den Bewirtschaftsungszeitraum 2021 - 2027 und 2050 nach Nutzergruppe (Öffentliche Wasserversorgung, Feldberegnung, Tierhaltende Betriebe, Industrie, Sonstige)  References: Schlattmann, A., Neuendorf, F., Burkhard, K. et al. (2022): Ecological Sustainability Assessment of Water Distribution for the Maintenance of Ecosystems, their Services and Biodiversity. Environmental Management 70, 329–349. https://doi.org/10.1007/s00267-022-01662-3.  Niedersächsisches Ministerium für Umwelt, Energie, Bauen und Klimaschutz (MU) 2021: Niedersächsischer Beitrag zu den Bewirtschaftungsplänen 2021 – 2027 der Flussgebiete Elbe, Weser, Ems und Rhein. Anhang B Grundwasser. Anhang B-1: Entnahmen aus Grundwasserkörpern. Datenbestand 04.07.2018. Datenherkunft: Elektronisches Wasserbuch.  Niedersächsisches Ministerium für Umwelt, Energie, Bauen und Klimaschutz (MU) (2022): Hintergrunddokument zum Wasserversorgungskonzept Niedersachsen. Online verfügbar unter https://www.umwelt.niedersachsen.de/download/183415/Hintergrunddokument_zum_Wasserversorgungskonzept_Niedersachsen.pdf, zuletzt geprüft am 29.10.2024.  Autorenzugehörigkeit / Author affiliation: Ole Badelt: Institute of Environmental Planning (IUP), Leibniz University Hannover".
