<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fk012w836>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "ZWD analysis Nevada Hongkong UK".
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Analysis and figure-generation code for the study of a structure–amplitude relaxation precursor to convective initiation in GNSS zenith wet delay. From the wet delay we estimate two channels: a structure scale (λ, the spectral cutoff; smaller λ means longer, more coherent moisture structures) and an amplitude (σ). At rest the two are anti-correlated, and this coupling relaxes in the hours before convection. The repository contains the spectral estimator, the relaxation and temporal-lead tests, the coupled-fluctuation model, and the scripts that reproduce every figure, applied to three GNSS networks in contrasting regimes: continental (central United States), frontal-maritime (British Isles), and tropical (Hong Kong). Raw observations are not redistributed; only the derived structure-scale and amplitude products needed to reproduce the figures are included. Code under MIT, derived data under CC-BY-4.0.".
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad".
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-08-12T10:31:16.779224"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:31:16.779232"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/institut-fuer-meteorologie-und-klimatologie>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/zwd-analysis-nevada-hongkong-uk>.
<http://localhost:5002/2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:2835c1ff-f9ba-49fa-acbc-c9bda4dbf4ad.
<http://localhost:5002/e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fwj72f6ba>.
<http://localhost:5002/e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Data-based System Representation and Synchronization for Multiagent Systems".
<http://localhost:5002/e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "[*] Victor G. Lopez and Matthias A. Müller, \\'Data-based System Representation and Synchronization for Multiagent Systems\\'. Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Decision and Control 2024.  These codes simulate the solutions proposed in [*] for the data-based synchronization problem of homogeneous and heterogeneous agents. The file DBsynchronization_homogeneous.m corresponds to the method described in Section III for a multiagent system with one leader and three followers. This example was not shown in [*] for space reasons. The file DBsynchronization_heterogeneous.m uses the method in Section IV for a multiagent system with one leader and four followers, as shown in the paper.".
<http://localhost:5002/e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "e6e62585-aec5-4ac9-9f84-4b1d98eabe96".
