<http://localhost:5002/6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2F8dtqgzfi>.
<http://localhost:5002/6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "µCT data of an additively manufactured multi-material fused filament fabrication cube test specimen using metal-filled filaments".
<http://localhost:5002/6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset consists of micro-computed tomography (µCT) images of a multi-material cube test specimen additively manufactured using fused filament fabrication (FFF) and metal-filled filaments. The cube is composed of eight smaller cubes, alternating the materials.  * __Outer Dimensions:__ 20 x 20 x 20 mm³ (with each individual cube measuring 10 x 10 x 10 mm³)   * __Materials:__ colorFabb Steelfill and colorFabb Copperfill (PLA)  * __FFF Machine:__ Flashforge Creator Pro 2 (refer to the included .gx file for printing parameters)   * __µCT Scanner:__ Bruker SkyScan 1275   ![Cube Section](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/453889ca-498f-40a8-8c5e-801fd6be16a4/resource/744f527c-6ec9-4fc2-a3f0-5dda4b8344e5/download/cube_section.png)  ![Cube Slice](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/453889ca-498f-40a8-8c5e-801fd6be16a4/resource/4f9d64c6-6092-4a0b-abaf-ca66b55add76/download/cube_slice.jpg)  In the reconstructed cross-sectional CT images, the darker material represents the denser copper-filled filament.  ### Acknowledgments  * The project _“Computer tomograph for optomechatronic systems”_ was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) - Project number 432176896.".
<http://localhost:5002/6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "6cd4b4a1-9537-479b-a9be-c6311f4c9237".
