<http://localhost:5002/12cf2fed-0de2-4837-a841-d5095f1057a5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25835%2Fas534ng1>.
<http://localhost:5002/12cf2fed-0de2-4837-a841-d5095f1057a5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Optical Simulation of a Coaxial Flash LiDAR Concept".
<http://localhost:5002/12cf2fed-0de2-4837-a841-d5095f1057a5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The data refer to the optical simulation of a coaxial flash LiDAR concept performed using Ansys Zemax OpticaStudio. The concept is shown in the figure **Optical concept.png** attached below.  The coaxial optical path is realized with a polarizing beam splitter (PBS) and a quarter-wave plate (QWP), which together manipulate the polarization state of the laser beam. The simulation is performed for each subsystem according to its functionality.".
<http://localhost:5002/12cf2fed-0de2-4837-a841-d5095f1057a5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "12cf2fed-0de2-4837-a841-d5095f1057a5".
