<http://localhost:5002/b339646d-592d-4812-bacd-8c589bbfe072> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Copsil-Add-Gel-Rheology-Viscosity.7z".
<http://localhost:5002/b339646d-592d-4812-bacd-8c589bbfe072> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-rheology-data-of-copsil-add-gel>.
<http://localhost:5002/b339646d-592d-4812-bacd-8c589bbfe072> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-rheology-data-of-copsil-add-gel>.
<http://localhost:5002/b339646d-592d-4812-bacd-8c589bbfe072> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "All measurements taken with Modular Compact Series of Anton Paar AG rheometer at Institut für Transport- und Automatisierungstechnik (ITA) of the Leibniz Universität Hannover (LUH).  All measurements taken by Lennart Mesecke @IPeG under supervision of Tobias Biermann @IPeG.  All measurements taken at roomtemperature R_T=20°C.   The material was analyzed regarding viscosity und shear stress under given shear rates.   Test series A contains measurements with shearrates from 0-200 1/s. B contains measurements with shearrates from 0-50 1/s, focussing on lower shear rates.  The analyses file contains the evaluated Herschel-Bulkley-parameters. Please note, that the Herschel-Bulkley-parameters unsufficiently fit the measurement data due to wall-slip effects during the measurements.  The measurements therefore should be viewed with caution, since wall-slip effect leads to underestimating the yield stress of the material.".
