<http://localhost:5002/f8087ecf-63d0-49e2-b9e4-01becd2801a6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/f8087ecf-63d0-49e2-b9e4-01becd2801a6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "BC (0,0): state #2 in sector (0,0)".
<http://localhost:5002/f8087ecf-63d0-49e2-b9e4-01becd2801a6> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/f8087ecf-63d0-49e2-b9e4-01becd2801a6> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/f8087ecf-63d0-49e2-b9e4-01becd2801a6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the even length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=0,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(0,0).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two. In addition, we have 2 real roots at level-1. On the level-2 we have one extra real root and one extra root with imag. part pi.  * this state is a descendant * the subleading corrections to scaling are power laws".
