<http://localhost:5002/f2995b99-2aae-4129-b9cb-908d9816565d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "BC (0,0): state #? in sector (2,1)".
<http://localhost:5002/f2995b99-2aae-4129-b9cb-908d9816565d> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/f2995b99-2aae-4129-b9cb-908d9816565d> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/f2995b99-2aae-4129-b9cb-908d9816565d> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the odd length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=0,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(2,1).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two. In addition, we have one level-1 root with an imaginary part pi/2.  * the subleading corrections to scaling are power laws".
