<http://localhost:5002/d08b7c38-9e7c-4fc7-929e-71d552d79e91> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the odd length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=1,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(1,0).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two. In addition we have two root on level-1 on the line i pi/2, one real level-2 root and one level-2 root on the line i pi. * this state is second excited state from a continuum of states in this sector in the thermodynamic limit * the subleading corrections to scaling are logarithmic".
