<http://localhost:5002/4981a059-8796-428a-bc56-4be9297917be> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the even length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=1,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(1,0).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two. In addition we have three root on level-1 on the line i pi/2, two real level-2 root and one level-2 root on the line i pi. * this state is second excited state from a continuum of states in this sector in the thermodynamic limit * the subleading corrections to scaling are logarithmic".
