<http://localhost:5002/32970e85-8c15-4e0e-b364-eabbb30e9bc2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the even length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=1,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(1,1).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two, in addition we have a real level-1 root.       pi/6<gamma<pi/4:  * this state is the lowest state from a continuum of states in this sector in the thermodynamic limit * the subleading corrections to scaling are logarithmic  gamma<pi/6:   * this state becomes a discrete state below the continuum of states  * the subleading corrections to scaling are power laws".
