<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "BC (1,0): class A-state #1 in sector (2,0)".
<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-bethe-ansatz-data-for-the-open-d_3-2-spin-chain>.
<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the even length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=1,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(2,0).  pi/8<\\gamma<pi/4:   * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two * this state is the lowest continuum state in this sector in the thermodynamic limit, it is the ground state for pi/8<gamma<\\pi/6 * the subleading corrections to scaling are logarithmic  \\gamma<\\pi/8:  * the state is discrete.  * the corrections to scaling are power law".
<http://localhost:5002/495a390e-ba5c-4d25-ba69-f8b26202c5cb> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "2635137"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
