<http://localhost:5002/fb0af5c4-5300-4e0e-8dfa-ee3190a35a31> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Bethe roots for a state of the even length D^{(2)}_3 spin chain with boundary conditions (epsilon=1,p=0) in the sector (h_1,h_2)=(2,1).  * the root configuration consists of complex conjugate pairs with imag. part (\\pi/2-\\gamma) on level one, pi/2 on level two, we have an additional level-1 root with imaginary part of pi/2. * this state is the lowest continuum state in this sector in the thermodynamic limit * the subleading corrections to scaling are logarithmic".
