<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "brdf_data_spectral.csv".
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-spectral-brdf-measurements-and-fitted-reflection-model-parameters-of-ten-urban-materials>.
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-spectral-brdf-measurements-and-fitted-reflection-model-parameters-of-ten-urban-materials>.
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Spectrally resolved BRDF values in inverse steradian (1/sr) in wide format. Each row is a measured combination of incident and outgoing direction, given by their polar (θ) and azimuthal (φ) angles in degrees together with the material key. Spectral BRDF data are given in multiple columns with each wavelength bin being a separate column. The 99 bin columns are named by their center wavelength in nanometers (e.g., w500 covers 497.5–502.5 nm), with a bin width of 5 nm below 750 nm and 10 nm above.".
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "9087189"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "CSV".
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-07-28T11:39:10.765926"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/404fe523-47d8-40f0-9a81-cb49991de186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:20:58.222660"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "reflection_model_parameters.csv".
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-spectral-brdf-measurements-and-fitted-reflection-model-parameters-of-ten-urban-materials>.
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-spectral-brdf-measurements-and-fitted-reflection-model-parameters-of-ten-urban-materials>.
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Per-material reflection model parameters, with one row per material. The surface albedo ρ is computed directly from the measurements by numerical integration, while the model parameters are fitted by minimizing the weighted normalized RMSE (NRMSEw). Model parameters are given for the Lambertian model (fitting error only), the Phong model (diffuse albedo ρ_d, specular albedo ρ_s, and specular exponent n), the energy-preserving Oren-Nayar model (roughness r), and the Phong+Oren-Nayar superposition (ρ_s, n, ρ_eon, r), each with its associated NRMSEw. The albedo and all model parameters are dimensionless; the NRMSEw is given in inverse steradian (1/sr).".
<http://localhost:5002/45e4a830-9478-4d9f-b9d0-be29fbb10723> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "1131"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
