<http://localhost:5002/1fa6e275-716b-4573-94e6-ed29f88d7d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "The Machine and Tool Ontology (MATO)".
<http://localhost:5002/1fa6e275-716b-4573-94e6-ed29f88d7d71> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-machine-and-tool-ontology>.
<http://localhost:5002/1fa6e275-716b-4573-94e6-ed29f88d7d71> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-machine-and-tool-ontology>.
<http://localhost:5002/1fa6e275-716b-4573-94e6-ed29f88d7d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Machine and Tool Ontology (MATO) represents a semantic model for the general description of equipment used in the development of production technologies. The equipment is described by properties like manufacturer, model, physical location, and a specific application area, as well as by using freely formulated expressions in natural language. MATO enables the expression of possible combinations of different equipment types required to fulfill a specific action. Furthermore, MATO semantically relates equipment with agents such as persons and organizations responsible for them.".
