<http://localhost:5002/c62d3b59-0f16-43fb-8a16-f53ed4d9edc7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Szenariendaten Windenergie (Variante 2, [EE100-konkret](https://www.bfn.de/sites/default/files/2021-09/Skript614.pdf)): Nennleistung und Energieerzeugung je Planungsregion, Szenarienjahr 2050   Felder der Shapedatei: * „leistung“: Leistung in MW * „energy“: Energieertrag (Szenarienjahr 2050, Wetterjahr 2012) in MWh/a  * „name“: Name der Planungsregion".
<http://localhost:5002/c62d3b59-0f16-43fb-8a16-f53ed4d9edc7> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "4000808"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/c62d3b59-0f16-43fb-8a16-f53ed4d9edc7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "ZIP".
<http://localhost:5002/c62d3b59-0f16-43fb-8a16-f53ed4d9edc7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2021-11-12T13:30:51.825855"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/c62d3b59-0f16-43fb-8a16-f53ed4d9edc7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:33.764779"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/9fe743d3-91c0-4aca-8ca8-d1e8b692157f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/9fe743d3-91c0-4aca-8ca8-d1e8b692157f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "deposit zwd_precursor".
<http://localhost:5002/9fe743d3-91c0-4aca-8ca8-d1e8b692157f> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-zwd-turbulence-precursor_v2>.
<http://localhost:5002/9fe743d3-91c0-4aca-8ca8-d1e8b692157f> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-zwd-turbulence-precursor_v2>.
<http://localhost:5002/9fe743d3-91c0-4aca-8ca8-d1e8b692157f> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Zenith wet delay turbulence precursor of tropical-cyclone convection (v2)  Derived data and analysis code for the manuscript “Dense navigation-satellite networks time water-vapour reorganization hours before tropical cyclone convection”.  DOI of this deposit: https://doi.org/10.25835/9rps2gis Author names removed for peer review.  Contents  DATA/<storm>_sea.npz : per-storm superposed-epoch arrays. hrs is time in hours from closest approach; lam and lam_s the raw and smoothed cut-off frequency in s^-1; sig the unsmoothed fluctuation amplitude in mm; lbase and sbase the pre-storm baselines. DATA/<storm>_zwd.npz : network-median zenith wet delay on the same grid. DATA/stations/<site>/*_maternfit.csv : per-station, per-day estimates. Columns: window-centre epoch (MJD), lambda (s^-1), sigma (m), quality flag. DATA/tracks/storm_<name>.json : best-track geometry, closest-approach time and distance for each cyclone. QUIET/ : the storm-free summer record behind the false-alarm rate. CODE/ : spectral estimator, onset and detector definitions, statistics and figure scripts. SOURCE_DATA/ : one CSV per storm, as required by the journal.  Spectral estimator  Matern/von Karman spectrum with the slope parameter fixed at alpha = 1.3, so that only the cut-off frequency and the amplitude are estimated. Sliding windows of 62.5 min (125 samples at 30 s), stride 5 min, Slepian tapers (NW = 4, K = 7), debiased Whittle likelihood. Two detrend stages: a global Savitzky-Golay of order 3 over 125.5 min, then a first-order detrend inside each window.  Raw observations  Raw GNSS observations are not redistributed here. Hong Kong SatRef data are available from the Hong Kong Geodetic Survey after free registration; NOAA CORS data are openly available from the NOAA National Geodetic Survey.  Licence  Data under CC BY 4.0, code under the MIT licence".
