<http://localhost:5002/528ca2f8-f447-4a96-b742-f9d293ca6171> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-datasets-for-classification-and-regression-in-human-robot-interaction-with-parallel-robots>.
<http://localhost:5002/528ca2f8-f447-4a96-b742-f9d293ca6171> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "# Classification of Collided-Body Classification  This project deals with the collided-body classification. The goal is to determine the collided body of a parallel robot which can be one of its six links or the end-effector platform. More information can be found in the publication [https://doi.org/10.1109/IROS55552.2023.10342345](10.1109/IROS55552.2023.10342345)  ## Project Structure  The project directory contains the following files:  -   `main.py`: The main Python script. It loads the training and test data and visualizes the data by generating three distinct 3D scatter plots for EE pose, distances and angles. -   `train.csv`: The training dataset. Contains time-series data from the robot, including joint angles, end-effector coordinates, forces, and torques. This data is used to train a classification model. -   `test.csv`: The test dataset. It has the same structure as `train.csv` and is used to evaluate the performance of the trained model.   ## Data Description  The `.csv` files contain the following variables:  -   **`t_s`**: Time (s) -   **`q_des_deg_[1-9]`**: Target joint angle for joints 1-9 (deg) -   **`q_deg_[1-9]`**: Actual joint angle for joints 1-9 (deg) -   **`x_des_m_rad_[1-3]`**: Target end-effector pose (x, y, orientation) (m, deg) -   **`x_m_rad_[1-3]`**: Actual end-effector position (x, y, orientation) (m, deg) -   **`tau_qa_Nm_[1-3]`**: Actual motor torque for motors 1-3 (Nm) -   **`tau_ext_fts_Nm_[1-3]`**: External torque projected from force-torque sensor (Nm) -   **`tau_ext_est_Nm_[1-3]`**: Estimated external torque (Nm) -   **`F_ext_fts_N_Nm_[1-6]`**: External forces (1-3) and moments (4-6) from sensor. The third component represents the link-orthogonal force. (N, Nm) -   **`F_ext_fts_proj_mobPlat_CS0_N_Nm_[1-3]`**: Measured and projected external force and moment on the mobile end-effector platform in base frame (N, Nm) -   **`F_ext_est_mobPlat_CS0_N_Nm_[1-3]`**: Estimated external force and moment on the mobile end-effector platform in base frame (N, Nm) -   **`distances_m_[1-3]`**: Distances for classification (m) -   **`angles_deg_[1-3]`**: Angles for classification (deg) -   **`collided_body`**: Identifier for the body in contact (1-6=links, 7=platform) (-)  ## Execution  To run the main script and display the visualization, ensure you have Python and the following libraries installed:  -   pandas -   numpy -   matplotlib  You can install the required libraries using pip:  ```bash pip install pandas numpy matplotlib ```  Then, run the script from your terminal:  ```bash python main.py ```  The script will load the data and display three 3D plots.".
