<http://localhost:5002/4656bcac-ee1a-45c5-a8f9-6f3476071e69> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-datasets-for-classification-and-regression-in-human-robot-interaction-with-parallel-robots>.
<http://localhost:5002/4656bcac-ee1a-45c5-a8f9-6f3476071e69> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "# Classification of Contact-Type  This project deals with the classification of contact types (collision/clamping). More information can be found in the publication [https://doi.org/10.1109/IROS55552.2023.10341581](10.1109/IROS55552.2023.10341581)  ## Project Structure  The project directory contains the following files:  -   `main.py`: The main Python script. It loads the training and test data and visualizes the data by generating three distinct 3D scatter plots for end-effector pose, distances and estimated external forces. -   `train.csv`: The training dataset. Contains time-series data from the robot, including joint angles, end-effector coordinates, forces, and torques. This data can used to train a classification model. -   `test.csv`: The test dataset. It has the same structure as `train.csv` and is used to evaluate the performance of the trained model.   ## Data Description  The `.csv` files contain the following variables:  -   **`t_s`**: Time (s) -   **`q_des_deg_[1-9]`**: Target joint angle for joints 1-9 (deg) -   **`q_deg_[1-9]`**: Actual joint angle for joints 1-9 (deg) -   **`x_des_m_rad_[1-3]`**: Target end-effector pose (x, y, orientation) (m, deg) -   **`x_m_rad_[1-3]`**: Actual end-effector pose (x, y, orientation) (m, deg) -   **`tau_qa_Nm_[1-3]`**: Actual motor torque for motors 1-3 (Nm) -   **`tau_ext_fts_Nm_[1-3]`**: External torque from sensor (Nm) -   **`tau_ext_est_Nm_[1-3]`**: Estimated external torque (Nm) -   **`F_ext_est_mobPlat_CS0_N_Nm_[1-3]`**: Estimated external force and moment on the mobile end-effector platform in base frame (N, Nm) -   **`distances_m_[1-3]`**: Distances for classification (m) -   **`angles_deg_[1-3]`**: Angles for classification (deg) -   **`clamping_collision`**: Identifier for the type of contact (0=collision, 1=clamping) (-)  ## Execution  To run the main script and display the visualization, ensure you have Python and the following libraries installed:  -   pandas -   numpy -   matplotlib  You can install the required libraries using pip:  ```bash pip install pandas numpy matplotlib ```  Then, run the script from your terminal:  ```bash python main.py ```  The script will load the data and display three 3D plots.".
