<http://localhost:5002/cb0b18a9-7247-4df0-bfd1-75f04e54c829> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BETA -> values of wave damping coefficient Beta for all wave runs and mat configurations DATA -> measured wave and velocity data at each USS and ADV position. All single measurements are included in this table M0 -> same data as DATA but just for the control experiments (M0) M1 -> same data as DATA but just for the 1-mat experiments (M1) M2 -> same data as DATA but just for the 2-mat experiments (M2)".
<http://localhost:5002/cb0b18a9-7247-4df0-bfd1-75f04e54c829> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "70078"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/cb0b18a9-7247-4df0-bfd1-75f04e54c829> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "mat".
<http://localhost:5002/cb0b18a9-7247-4df0-bfd1-75f04e54c829> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:35:15.927817"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/cb0b18a9-7247-4df0-bfd1-75f04e54c829> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.256468"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "All Calculated Parameters".
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Data containing all parameters calculated and used in Figures 4,5,6 and 11 in Villanueva et al 2023.   M0, M1 and M2 contain the same data as DATA, separated by mat configuration  DATA: Hr -> Wave height ratio to position 1 (leading edge of canopy) uc -> steady flow component of measured orbital velocity uw -> wave velocity rms (suffix) -> root mean square min -> minimum max -> maximum a1M0 (suffix) -> alternative calculation based on value measured for the control experiments (no vegetation) at ADV1 ratio (suffix) -> ratio of max and min (absolute value) om -> circular frequency omega A0 -> wave orbital velocity amplitude A1 (suffix) -> ratio to leading edge value (ADV1) of same measurement alpha -> flow attenuation parameter. The 2 subsequent digits indicate the positions for the ratio caluclatio. e.g. 13 = ratio between values measured at postions 1 and 3 *_red_* -> velocity reduction in percent [%]. positive indicates velocitiy increase. The 2 subsequent digits indicate the positions for the velocity change. e.g. 13 = ratio between values measured at postions 1 and 3 A_S_ratio -> A0/S where S is the stem separation l_eff -> effecive length (see Villanueva et al. 2022) *_r_* -> ratio m (suffix) -> mean e (suffix) -> error KC -> Keulegan-Carpenter Number Re -> Reynolds Number Re_bv -> stem-based Re C_D -> Drag Coefficient Beta -> damping coefficient for C_D and Beta, the suffixes are as follows: 	flat -> fixed value  	C_D_villa -> value calculated by Villanueva et al. 2022 	losa -> value calculated following Losada et al. 2016 	dalr -> following Dalrymple et al. 1984 	Lei -> value after Lei and Nepf 2019b L -> Wavelength".
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "54245"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:39:27.809166"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/f9833d9e-83c0-428f-992d-128ec55f5ee9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.256605"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Wave Decay (Damping Coefficient)".
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The datasets here contain the calculated wave decay data (beta in Villanueva et al. 2023, see Figure 3).  Each data set contains tables for all mat configurations and ADV positions such that the different datasets differ in wave condition only. See Nomenclature for naming convention.   Within each .MAT file the following information can be found: TABLES: H_r -> ratio of wave height to incident wave height at position 1. Data at each z-position (ADV height)  PA -> Phase Average Hr_m -> ratio of wave height to incident wave height at position 1. Mean and standard deviation of all measurements (z-positions)  STRUCTURES: PhaseAvg_full -> phase averaged data for each USS and Mat configuration 	NoSample -> number of samples used during for the bins phase averaging  Hr_ASG -> x position (see experimental set-up) and ratios used to fit equation 1 (Villanueva et al, 2023)  Hr_fits -> beta (damp_Coeff) and fit coefficients".
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "1591550"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "zip, mat".
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:15:34.002065"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/8ee1f090-d3df-40f4-b8ed-f03b4ac98d71> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.256722"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Velocity Structure (Orbital Velocities)".
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The datasets here contain the calculated velocity structure data (see Figure 7 in Villanueva et al. 2023).  Each data set contains a structure for all mat configurations and ADV positions such that the different datasets differ in wave condition only. See Nomenclature for naming convention.   Within each .MAT file the following information can be found: VARIABLES: d -> depth condition x -> x-position (see experimental set-up) WC_m -> wave condition (first value is T and second value is H)  STRUCTURES: ADV_z -> all preliminary post-processed (first step after raw) data of the ADV at each x and z position  M0,M1,M2 -> data for each mat configuration and ADV showing the phase average, time-synchronous average, wave root mean sqaure velocity, current component".
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "427831689"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "zip,mat".
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:22:23.040297"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/00670dc3-3356-43fc-b739-22314253a129> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.256837"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Time Series of Flow Attenuation Parameter (alpha)".
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In this folder there are several .MAT files with the time series (TS) of A/S and alpha_w for the curves based on Lowe et al. (2005). My curves match those of the authors within the inertia-dominated (left) and general flow areas, but not within the unidirectional flow section, as the curves all kind of converge there.   The data used for the publication (Figure 10 in Villanueva et al. 2023) comes from A_S_vs_Alpha_lambda. See below for a description of the contents of the .MAT file  I wanted to find out to what parameters the curves were sensitive, therefore, varying the parameters in the suffix of each name here, I created different datasets of TS.   RESULTS: Interestingly, the curves are not at all sensitive to the wave period T. The only change observable for longer periods is that the curve started changing values at A/S higher (above 10^0), but then followed almost the same path.  C_D barely made a change, shifting the curve at higher A/S values up or down slightly, but not separated from each other (recall that the authors used the same C_D for all experiments).   C_M controls alpha_w in the inertia limit  d did not have any effect  C_f has the most marked effect. Especially since the plant parameters dont change. Remeber that in the unidirectional limit, the ratio alpha reduces to sqrt(Ld/Ls)  If you want the curves to look exactly like those obtained by Lowe et al (2005), you need to use their plant values (changing S and d) and the varying C_f.   CONTENTS of the .MAT file(s) d -> depth H -> Wave Height h_c -> canopy height S -> stem separation t_v -> plant thickness TS -> (structure) Time Series  	Sd_ratio = S/d 	b_v -> plant width 	C_f -> friction coefficient 	alpha -> flow attenuation parameter 	A_S_ratio -> time series of A/S  U -> generic Velocity Time Series z -> height of alpha calculation".
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "28250760"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/format> "ZIP".
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:34:10.361792"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/4035cd2a-fc87-4bfb-89dd-8d812e4e8064> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.256947"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Statistical values of calculated alpha".
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Data supporting Figure 9 in Villanueva et al. 2023  variables are disambiguated and compared to each other. Param_Table (DATA) is used as base and the data extracted in different tables shown here, where the variable name indicates the variables and positions compared.  d -> depth, with values being 1,2, and 3 corresponding to depth 1,2 and 3 as described in the paper.  H -> Wave Height, with values showing ranges in cm after \\'H\\' T -Y Wave Period, with values showing the period in seconds after \\'T\\'  suffixes (after the underscore) correspond to the alpha ratio calculation positions, e.g. 14 means that the velocity at position 4 was divided by that at position 1, thus obtaining the flow attenuation between positions 1 and 4, or alpha_w,1-4 in the figure.".
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#byteSize> "56594"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023-06-27T14:36:05.614177"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/936fe65d-7859-41b9-abcb-950f2fa0272b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-08-12T10:18:45.257053"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/e62648d8-4a6e-40c4-a482-628791856ef8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Distribution>.
<http://localhost:5002/e62648d8-4a6e-40c4-a482-628791856ef8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Canopy-integrated velocities".
<http://localhost:5002/e62648d8-4a6e-40c4-a482-628791856ef8> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-seagrasswavedynamics_rv>.
