<http://localhost:5002/68a134a1-8e93-4656-94f5-6a546e784638> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Camera image evaluation results for 7 x 3816 repetitions of the seven measurement scenarios presented in the manuscript (see extended data figure 1).  Each line contains: * image number * measurement scenario number * camera count value mF=+1, after subtraction of systematic effects * camera count value mF=0, raw values * camera count value mF=-1, after subtraction of systematic effects * quantized atom number mF=+1 * quantized atom number mF=0 * quantized atom number mF=-1 * camera count value mF=+1, raw values * camera count value mF=+1, raw values  Note that for the mF=+/-1 camera count values two systematic effects were subtracted (\\'signal leakage\\' from mF=0 atoms and a drifting background value), as described in the Methods section. This is why the values are non-integers.".
