<http://localhost:5002/b1ce9761-03c4-4d45-99a5-bbcd5a6daf8b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "randomsampled_occurrence_data_for_entanglement_depth_calculation.zip".
<http://localhost:5002/b1ce9761-03c4-4d45-99a5-bbcd5a6daf8b> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-data-suporting-publication-hong-ou-mandel-interference-of-more-than-10-indistinguishable-atoms>.
<http://localhost:5002/b1ce9761-03c4-4d45-99a5-bbcd5a6daf8b> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#downloadURL> <http://localhost:5002/luh-data-suporting-publication-hong-ou-mandel-interference-of-more-than-10-indistinguishable-atoms>.
<http://localhost:5002/b1ce9761-03c4-4d45-99a5-bbcd5a6daf8b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Random sampled occurrence data for the uncertainty estimation of the entanglement depth values k. The underlying probability distributions are multinomial distributions of the Jz values, with the size being the sample number, and the probabilities being the measured frequencies. Each line contains a random sample of the Twin-Fock state Jz occurrences, and the HB state Jz occurrences (Jx of TF). These samples are used to determine a value k, either by the novel criterion based on parity or by the \\'old one\\' based on the variance of Jz. The k values in the manuscript are the mean values, where the displayed error bars are given by asymmetric standard deviations of these k-value samples (see Methods).".
